WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:10.040
"Please pardon the interruption. Attention
all students and staff. Please initiate internal

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:18.370
lockdown procedure at this time. I repeat.
Please initiate internal lockdown procedure

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.460
at this time."

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:28.140
Hello, and welcome to Al Dente Creepypasta,
horror stories cooked to perfection with a

00:00:28.149 --> 00:00:36.829
splash of red sauce. My name is CZ and I will
be your server, this episode. Break is now

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:43.620
over which means it’s time to get back to
Creepy Clown School Lockdown. Let’s dig

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.820
right in.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.400
I had been waiting all year for the floor
hockey unit in gym. This year I was out for

00:00:58.409 --> 00:01:03.239
blood. There's this kid at my school, Callum,
who thinks he's just the greatest thing that

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:08.510
ever happened to any of us. He plays on a
traveling ice hockey team, so every year when

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:13.409
we get to the hockey unit, he single handedly
outclasses everyone. But that's not enough

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:19.799
for Callum. Oh no, he has to show off, use
all his fancy little tricks. His team wins

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:26.140
every single game and he makes it look easy,
like he's not even interested in trying. As

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.640
if his cocky attitude wasn't already a good
enough reason for me not to like him, the

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.140
girls just swoon over him, and of course,
he acts like he doesn't care.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:41.579
Well, me and my friend Geo got tired of being
effortlessly shown up by this pretty-boy,

00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:46.890
so we've practicing in his driveway just about
every free day we get. We may not know any

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:52.899
of his fancy little tricks, but I think we're
physically on a level to compete. To add motivation,

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:57.409
there's a girl I like named Kelsey in our
gym class, so I couldn't afford to be embarrassed

00:01:57.409 --> 00:01:59.909
by Callum if I go all out.

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:04.590
On our first day of floor hockey, we were
broken up into 8 teams. I led my team to three

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:09.000
undefeated matches before it was time to face
Callum's team, who was also undefeated at

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.530
the time. My heart was racing as I walked
up to the line, though I didn't let onto it.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:20.370
Callum just had a bored disinterested look
on his face. Good. Maybe I'd take him by surprise.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:26.420
N. H. L. I tried to sweep the puck away from
the face off but Callum was too quick. I took

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:30.400
a defensive position. He cooly brought up
the puck to challenge me, leaving it out in

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.190
front of him for me to try to snatch it away.
I didn't take the bait, so he scooped the

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:38.500
puck off the floor of the field house. Seeing
my chance, I knocked his stick away, and seized

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.370
the puck. I was already taking off in the
other direction. I easily deked around the

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:46.630
rest of his team and deposited a shot in the
back of the net. 1-0.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:50.911
I won the next face-off. I lobbed the puck
into an empty corner and chased it down. With

00:02:50.911 --> 00:02:55.730
one man to beat, I deflected a shot off of
him and into the goal. 2-0.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:00.300
Callum and I got back to the center circle.
He had that same bored look on his face. I

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:04.261
could tell if I won he was going to try to
play it off like he was never trying. But

00:03:04.261 --> 00:03:09.520
he and I... and Kelsey for that matter, knew
he had gone undefeated in the other matches.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:15.310
Plus, I had one more trick up my sleeve to
really put him in his place. I won the faceoff

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:20.840
again, this time I went right for Callum and
challenged him directly. Suddenly, he looked

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.730
surprised. Without looking down I sent the
puck in between his legs and dashed around

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:29.190
the side of him. As the puck got by him, and
safely into my possession I couldn't help

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:33.940
but crack a little bit of a smile with nothing
but an open path to the goal.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:38.510
That's when I felt something hook my legs,
and I went crashing down onto my face as the

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:43.930
puck slid away into the corner. Callum. He
had reached back with his stick and intentionally

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:49.510
taken me out. Going face first into the ground
and slamming down my knee hurt, but I could

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:55.590
take that. But hearing Callum's cocky, defiant,
"oops" and seeing Kelsey unable to stop her

00:03:55.590 --> 00:04:02.020
mouth from falling open in laughter set me
over. Ears burning, I got to my feet. Forgetting

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:07.590
about the puck, the game, and where I was,
I socked Callum straight in the jaw.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:11.150
Before he could retaliate, our gym teacher
had yanked me away from the game and his face

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:16.310
was red as he screamed in my face. I didn't
hear any of it. My mind was still racing with

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.480
anger.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:22.450
I found myself sitting outside the athletic
office before I'd started to calm down. Callum

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:26.110
was sitting on the far side of the room. I
should have been happy that he was getting

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:30.979
punished too, but he had this dumb smirk on
his face. Somehow I knew my parents were going

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:35.979
to be a lot more upset than his when all was
said and done. We sat in silence for a few

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:39.889
minutes before, an announcement came over
the intercom.

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:46.340
"Please pardon the interruption. Attention
students and staff. Please initiate internal

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.780
lockdown procedure at this time."

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:55.080
Now, normally I wouldn't have cared to participate
in a lockdown drill. But there was something

00:04:55.180 --> 00:05:00.879
about this. Maybe that little hint of tremble
in the principal's voice. I think Callum felt

00:05:00.879 --> 00:05:03.419
it too. Felt that it could be real.

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:06.820
"What should we do?" I asked him, breaking
the silence.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.370
"Uhh I dunno."

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:12.130
It didn't seem like he was going to cooperate,
but then he added, "should we go look for

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:13.590
Mr. Dyke?"

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:18.620
Mr. Dyke was our gym teacher, a huge, hulking
mass of muscle, and probably the safest person

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:23.229
in the school to be around at a time like
this. I told Callum, "OK," and we headed back

00:05:23.229 --> 00:05:24.800
into the halls by the locker room.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:29.189
All of the lights had been shut off, so the
only source of light was coming from the door

00:05:29.189 --> 00:05:34.189
at our end of the hall. All the way at the
opposite end, there's a closet. The door was

00:05:34.189 --> 00:05:39.150
open, and someone was standing inside, facing
the inside of the closet. Callum looked like

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:43.879
he was about to call out, but I threw my hand
up as if to say, 'hold on'. He froze and eyed

00:05:43.879 --> 00:05:44.879
me.

00:05:44.879 --> 00:05:48.689
I wanted to make sure we weren't about to
willingly give ourselves up to the intruder.

00:05:48.689 --> 00:05:54.819
We quietly walked in to get a better look
and see if we knew whoever was standing there.

00:05:54.819 --> 00:05:56.919
*footsteps*

00:05:56.919 --> 00:06:01.360
As my eyes adjusted to the dark a little,
and as we got closer, the person started to

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:07.990
take shape. The figure had wide shoulders,
big ears, and short hair--- it was Mr. Dyke,

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:15.110
our teacher! Only, he was just staring into
a dark closet, shoulders shaking... no, trembling...

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:16.110
Something was off.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:21.659
"Mr. Dyke!" I called out. "We didn't know
what to do. Where should we..."

00:06:21.659 --> 00:06:28.180
But I trailed off when I realized that he
was not listening. He was just... like...

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:33.569
petrified at the opening of the equipment
closet. His whole body was trembling, he was

00:06:33.569 --> 00:06:36.710
breathing loudly and.... and he was whimpering.

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:39.849
"Mr. Dyke? ... Are you OK?"

00:06:39.849 --> 00:06:42.860
No response. He didn't even acknowledge us.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.120
Callum: "What the hell?"

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.560
"Come on. We need to go find another teacher."

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:52.340
We ran around the corner into the hall that
leads into the field house. One of the double

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:56.259
doors leading into the gym was cracked open
just slightly and I could see that the lights

00:06:56.259 --> 00:06:59.650
were off in there as well, other than this
faint orange glow.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.210
Callum: "Watch out."

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:05.789
There was some shattered glass on the floor.
I looked up to find someone had broken the

00:07:05.789 --> 00:07:10.889
glass cases next to the fire alarm and removed
the fire extinguisher and axe. Yeah, it's

00:07:10.889 --> 00:07:16.990
an old school. My heart dropped into my stomach.
This meant either one of two things. One,

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:22.939
that the threat was nearby and recently broke
in and retrieved the axe, or two, that someone

00:07:22.939 --> 00:07:27.710
was scared enough to retrieve the axe for
self defense. Neither boded well for Callum

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:28.710
and I.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:35.759
We went into the field house. The door swung
shut behind us.

00:07:35.759 --> 00:07:36.759
*doorclose*

00:07:36.759 --> 00:07:37.759
Callum: "Shoot."

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:42.090
He turned back and tried to open the door
we had just come through, but it was locked.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:46.389
The orange colored glow I had seen was coming
from the scoreboard. There was a timer on

00:07:46.389 --> 00:07:52.189
it, counting down with 1 minute and 33 seconds
remaining. There was also a score. It was

00:07:52.189 --> 00:07:58.020
0-0, but in place of the team names reading
home and away, the team names read ARIS vs

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.180
KIDS.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:03.819
We walked into the middle of the field house
and surveyed all around. The whole gym was

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:08.260
completely empty as far as I could tell. There
was one thought that sat in the back on my

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:12.720
mind though. There's this little room at the
top of the bleachers. It's where the scoreboard

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:18.319
control room is. From looking at the window,
I could tell the lights were off... but still...

00:08:18.319 --> 00:08:20.199
the scoreboard was on.

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:24.099
Naturally, we wanted to get out of there.
There are several exits on each side of the

00:08:24.099 --> 00:08:29.199
field house, but each one was locked. That
left us nothing to do but sit and wait for

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:31.340
the scoreboard timer to run out.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.340
*BUZZER*

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:45.340
The shot clock buzzer blasted out our eardrums,
as an insane, like I can't even describe the

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:49.500
horror, crazy clown crashed up against the
scoreboard room window with a violent force.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:55.690
This clown had a wild smile unlike anything
I had ever seen. The sound of that buzzer

00:08:55.690 --> 00:09:00.940
may have hit me hard, but the feeling of despair
when I laid eyes on that clown... that monstrous

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:08.460
sight, hit me ten times harder. A crackle
came over the announcer speaker and circus

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:14.980
music, no I am not making this up, distorted,
broken sounding circus music started playing.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:28.080
The scoreboard went off again. It now read
Aris: 1 Kids: 0 with no time remaining. The

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:33.020
door of the scoreboard room raucously flew
open and the clown, now holding an axe marched

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:38.090
it's big shoes into the doorway, the most
devilish grin on its face.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:44.460
The clown bounded down the bleachers towards
us laughing hysterically as he did so. I glanced

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:48.890
over at Callum, wondering if we were going
with fight or flight. To my surprise he had

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:53.560
already taken off and left me in the dust!
I turned to book it, but for the second time

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:59.140
that day I felt my center of balance disrupt
as a sideways hockey puck rolled me off of

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:03.990
my feet and I slammed into the ground yet
again. At this point, my knee was throbbing.

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:09.100
I tried to get up as quickly as I could, but
the pain was too much and the clown was already

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:15.100
hovering over me; it's grin stretching unnaturally
from ear to ear as it swung it's axe high

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:20.040
in the air.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:30.340
In those final moments, I found myself thinking
of some of my best and worst memories. My

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:39.071
birthday party at age seven. Getting in trouble
for sneaking alcohol with my friends. Opening

00:10:39.071 --> 00:10:48.450
my Nintendo DS on Christmas morning. And more...
It wasn't like my life flashing before my

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:55.410
eyes, like people talk about. It was more
of a scramble to find a final memory to hold

00:10:55.410 --> 00:11:02.280
onto. That's how I like to think of it. I
closed my eyes.

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:05.780
*clown screech*

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:11.200
My eyes shot back open to see what had caused
that horrible screech.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.310
Callum: Hyah!

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:17.971
The clown had somehow been knocked back by
something. I looked up, it was Callum! He

00:11:17.971 --> 00:11:22.340
was holding a hockey stick with the blade
turned away, using the butt end like a spear!

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:24.370
He jabbed at the clown's face knocking it
back.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.370
Callum: "Get back!"

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:29.880
I gingerly rose to my feet. Callum motioned
to the floor, where he had already dropped

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:34.510
a second hockey stick. These sticks had pretty
flimsy plastic blades, but using the opposite

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:38.020
end like Callum, we'd be able to pack a little
bit of a punch.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:42.690
The clown recomposed itself and approached
us again. It dragged the axe behind, leaving

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:47.020
an opening for us to try to make a quick attack.
But I knew better than to make a risky first

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:51.650
move. We waited until it was close enough
and let it take a wild unbalanced hack. I

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:56.220
felt my knee swelling as I jumped back out
of the way, but I was able to dodge the attack.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:12:00.780
I went in first and took a low slash at the
waist, then Callum got in close -- dangerously

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:05.190
close, what was he doing? He reared back and
with one stabbing motion, lodged his stick

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:08.340
into the clown’s eye socket!

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.240
*Clown screech*

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:14.810
My jaw dropped as Callum kept hold of the
other end of the hockey stick while the clown

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:20.090
crashed down on it’s back and writhed for
a moment before going limp.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:23.300
*clown writhing*

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:27.850
Callum yanked the stick out of the clown’s
head. Blood squirted everywhere. The clown’s

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:32.050
eye, which miraculously wasn’t crushed,
was ripped from its socket and bounced once

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:36.500
on the gym floor, still connected to the clown’s
head by a nerve like a ball and chain.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:42.520
I honestly didn’t know what to say at this
point. My knee was throbbing, and I felt like

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:47.640
I was going to throw up. I limped over to
the first row of the bleachers and sat down.

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:52.360
Callum just squatted on the floor. We sat
quietly, catching our breath and waited for

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:58.510
someone to find us. It was maybe 10 minutes
before the school police officer came in to

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:03.600
clear the room. We gave the entire story.
He insisted that we visit the nurse, which

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:08.560
I welcomed openly. Callum probably didn’t
need to checked out, but he went along anyway

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:12.800
-- figuring it was better than going back
to the office, though our little gym class

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:15.610
fight didn’t seem like such a big deal now.

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:19.320
The school nurse doesn’t have a ton of tools
at her disposal -- I was given an ice pack

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:24.240
for my knee and told to relax until the cops
showed up. While we waited, I apologized to

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:28.920
Callum for socking him in the face earlier,
and he told me he felt bad about his egregious

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:33.510
penalty as well. He said maybe he’d join
us for a little driveway hockey sometime and

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:36.340
he’d even let me have a penalty shot whenever
he does.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:41.350
I told him that was fair, but before he could
respond, another announcement came over the

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:44.940
intercom, only… it’s wasn’t the all-clear that 
I had expected.

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:50.920
"Attention all students and staff. You are
to remain in internal lockdown at this time.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:53.570
Please ensure ALL rooms are secure.”

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:58.320
The end of the announcement brought that uncomfortable
silence I had become all too familiar with

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:03.660
back into the room. The nurse went over and
locked the door. What was going on? Was there

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:07.640
a second intruder in the school? Normally
during a lockdown, we’d have to get against

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:11.730
the wall and hide on the ground away from
the windows. However, there were no windows

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:16.930
in the nurse’s office so we just stayed
where we were and remained silent.

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:18.980
*footsteps*

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:26.220
There were footsteps approaching down the
hall. I heard echoed screams coming from another

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:31.930
classroom. At least this time we were behind
a locked door. The steps continued to approach,

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:36.920
until the stopped in front of our door. I
held my breath.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:39.640
*rattle*

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:44.220
The person standing outside gave a hard tug
on our doorknob. It seemed like forever…

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:49.490
but realistically, it was a few more seconds
until the footsteps continued down the hall,

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:53.490
onto the next room. I let out a sigh of relief.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:57.290
About 30 minutes later, we would find out
the reason for the second announcement from

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:01.480
the police chief, who came to visit us at
the nurse’s office. After the school police

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:06.650
officer sent us on our way, he investigated
the clown, who appeared to be dead. He then

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:11.940
got word that the SWAT team had arrived, and
went to go touch base them. When they returned

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:16.150
to the field house and turned on the lights,
the body of the clown was no longer there.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:20.310
At that point, they made the second announcement,
making sure students and teachers did not

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:24.420
think that it was safe to come out of the
lockdown procedures. They had to re-clear

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:30.060
every single room, then after a meeting with
the administration staff, they finally decided

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:33.500
they had done everything they could do, and
finally gave the all-clear.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:37.850
There had been a couple of other clown attacks
at schools over the last couple years, so,

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:42.520
Callum and I were questioned heavily about
the incident. However, as you can imagine,

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:46.550
there were moments that caused them to roll
their eyes; they clearly didn’t believe

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:51.190
some of the more outlandish details. I’m
afraid that may have caused the validity of

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:56.080
our accounts to be thrown into question, but
everything in this story is the truth, and

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.940
I’ve got Callum to back me up on that.

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:01.010
But I let them know not to just take our word
for it.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:05.160
“Go find those hockey sticks we had used
to fend off the clown,” I told them. Of

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:09.990
course, they already had taken those in for
evidence, there was just one problem.

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:14.260
Some time over the next couple of weeks, they
ran tests on the DNA left behind on the sticks,

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:19.160
which matched the DNA of someone who had been
in a high security prison since 2016 and was

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:23.900
still there today. Obviously, I didn’t know
how this was possible, and they were coming

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:28.150
at me like I had planted this guy’s DNA
there, like this whole ordeal was some kind

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:32.640
of stupid prank we had pulled. I couldn’t
believe the way they were talking to me. So,

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:37.810
that was pretty much the end of that… but
unfortunately, it wasn’t the end of this

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:38.810
nightmare.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:43.860
There is one kind of cool thing about being
the victim of a lockdown attack. It got me

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:48.920
a lot of attention at school. For the next
two weeks, everyone wanted to hear my story…

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:54.360
and let’s just say I got pretty good retelling
my dramatic account for any of the cute girls

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:58.710
who asked me about it. Unfortunately, I was
never able to score that date with Kelsey

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:02.620
from gym class, but I had no shortage of female
attention.

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:06.890
One night I was walking home this girl -- I
think her name was Ashley. We were walking

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:11.199
because I didn’t have my license yet. We
walked by this alley, and out of the corner

00:17:11.199 --> 00:17:17.009
of my eye, I see someone standing there, staring
down the alley. Now... this next part happened

00:17:17.009 --> 00:17:22.659
pretty fast… and I’m still a little bit
unsure about it. I turned my head, and just

00:17:22.659 --> 00:17:28.760
before we walked past the alley, I catch a
brief glimpse of... the clown. The clown from

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:32.610
that day. Just standing there in the alley
-- one eye staring at me and the other eye

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:37.900
just hanging down out of it’s socket. My
heart FLIPPED.This can’t be happening. It

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:42.590
was over. Ashley, or whatever her name was,
stopped walking and asked me if I was OK.

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:49.480
I looked back, and… it was just an empty
alley. Nowhere to even hide. What was going

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:55.880
on? Was my mind playing tricks on me? Is this
was PTSD is like? I asked her if she saw anything,

00:17:55.880 --> 00:18:00.899
and she said no, but she was standing on the
other side of me, she couldn’t have…

00:18:00.899 --> 00:18:02.049
*sigh*

00:18:02.049 --> 00:18:05.389
Not wanting to look like a pussy in front
of my date I acted as if I had shrugged it

00:18:05.389 --> 00:18:09.850
off and changed the subject. But for the rest
of that night, I couldn’t get the sound

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:15.580
of that clown’s laughter out of my head.
In fact, I really can’t say with certainty

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:17.840
